course: dictionary
lesson: 6609
title: Normal: usual, healthy and expected
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Normal means usual, ordinary or expected: what happens most of the time. «A fever is when the body raises its temperature to fight infection; normal body temperature is about 36.5 to 37.5 degrees Celsius.» The word normal tells you the range you expect to see when a body is well.
explain: Normal can also mean healthy and as it should be. A temperature of 37 degrees is normal, but a fever is higher than normal. The words around normal give you the clue: «normal» sits next to temperature, body and fever, so it is about health.
explain: Feelings can be normal too. «Grief can come out as sadness, anger, tiredness, fear or even laughing; all of these are normal.» So if you feel strange after losing someone, that does not mean something is wrong with you. Look at the context: a story that says «not normal» is often hinting at a mystery or a problem.
fact: Normal means usual, ordinary or expected: what happens most of the time.
fact: Normal can also mean healthy and as it should be, such as a normal body temperature.
fact: «Back to normal» means the usual state again, after something has changed.
fact: «Normally» is the adverb: it means usually, most of the time.
fact: Chest pain or fainting during sport is never normal, so tell a grown-up straight away.
exercise: «A fever is when the body raises its temperature to fight infection; normal body temperature is about 36.5 to 37.5 degrees Celsius.» What does normal mean in this sentence? | *Healthy and as it should be | Loud and noisy | Only for adults | Very hot and dangerous
exercise: Mia says, «It is normal to feel worried before a test.» What does normal mean here? | *Usual and expected, something many people feel | Very loud and fast | It only happens once | Wrong and bad
exercise: In a story, the words «The house was not normal that night» are a clue. What do they suggest? | The night was cold and dry | *Something strange, perhaps a mystery or a problem | Everyone was fast asleep | The house was very clean
test: «Grief can come out as sadness, anger, tiredness, fear or even laughing; all of these are normal.» What does normal mean here? | Happy and calm | Only for grown-ups | *Expected, something many people feel | Dangerous and to be avoided
test: Which phrase means that things are usual again after a change? | very normal and loud | *back to normal | normal size and shape | normal in a hurry
exam: Which word fits the gap in «It ___ rains here in May, so bring a coat»? | normality | abnormal | *normally | normal
